{"module":"movements","voice":"male","duration":483.7,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Cómo ganaron los movimientos, y la estrategia para este","start":0.0,"end":3.53,"words":[[0.03,0.31],[0.31,0.79],[0.79,1.0],[1.0,1.83],[2.08,2.15],[2.15,2.28],[2.28,2.98],[2.98,3.25],[3.25,3.53]]},{"el":"intro","text":"El movimiento por los derechos civiles suele recordarse como unos cuantos grandes discursos.","start":4.33,"end":9.95,"words":[[4.34,4.47],[4.47,5.13],[5.13,5.33],[5.33,5.53],[5.53,6.05],[6.05,6.52],[6.52,6.85],[6.85,7.51],[7.51,7.77],[7.77,8.03],[8.03,8.5],[8.5,8.96],[8.96,9.62]]},{"el":"intro","text":"El registro muestra algo más útil: años de preparación, entrenamiento, organización local, demandas judiciales, cabildeo y presión económica, llevados a cabo por miles de personas comunes.","start":10.3,"end":23.53,"words":[[10.32,10.46],[10.46,11.01],[11.01,11.5],[11.5,11.78],[11.78,11.98],[11.98,12.33],[12.57,12.85],[12.85,12.99],[12.99,13.82],[14.06,15.04],[15.28,16.11],[16.11,16.53],[16.77,17.32],[17.32,18.09],[18.33,18.89],[18.89,18.95],[18.95,19.44],[19.44,20.13],[20.38,20.86],[20.86,20.93],[20.93,21.21],[21.21,21.42],[21.42,21.76],[21.76,21.9],[21.9,22.46],[22.46,23.01]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Cada uno de esos métodos puede usarse para aprobar una Ley CAREN federal.","start":23.88,"end":28.59,"words":[[23.91,24.18],[24.18,24.37],[24.37,24.5],[24.5,24.77],[24.77,25.23],[25.23,25.55],[25.55,25.95],[25.95,26.21],[26.21,26.67],[26.67,26.87],[26.87,27.06],[27.06,27.39],[27.39,27.92]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Montgomery: primero la preparación, luego la presión","start":28.94,"end":32.72,"words":[[28.97,29.73],[29.98,30.47],[30.47,30.61],[30.61,31.45],[31.69,32.04],[32.04,32.18],[32.18,32.67]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Rosa Parks no estaba simplemente cansada cuando se negó a ceder su asiento el 1 de diciembre de 1955.","start":33.42,"end":41.61,"words":[[33.42,33.71],[33.71,34.06],[34.06,34.2],[34.2,34.63],[34.63,35.42],[35.42,35.91],[35.91,36.34],[36.34,36.48],[36.48,36.77],[36.77,36.84],[36.84,37.2],[37.2,37.34],[37.34,37.84],[37.84,37.98],[37.98,38.19],[38.19,38.34],[38.34,38.98],[38.98,39.12],[39.12,41.26]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Era la secretaria de la NAACP local y ese verano se había capacitado en organización comunitaria en la Highlander Folk School.","start":41.96,"end":50.18,"words":[[41.96,42.18],[42.18,42.33],[42.33,43.09],[43.09,43.24],[43.24,43.39],[43.39,43.77],[43.77,44.14],[44.14,44.22],[44.22,44.44],[44.44,44.9],[44.9,45.05],[45.05,45.43],[45.43,46.18],[46.18,46.33],[46.33,47.24],[47.24,48.07],[48.07,48.22],[48.22,48.37],[48.37,48.97],[48.97,49.27],[49.27,49.8]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Jo Ann Robinson y el Consejo Político de Mujeres llevaban meses planeando un boicot; imprimieron decenas de miles de volantes en una sola noche.","start":50.53,"end":60.02,"words":[[50.55,50.69],[50.69,50.91],[50.91,51.5],[51.5,51.57],[51.57,51.72],[51.72,52.24],[52.24,52.82],[52.82,52.97],[52.97,53.48],[53.48,54.0],[54.0,54.37],[54.37,55.03],[55.03,55.17],[55.17,55.69],[55.94,56.75],[56.75,57.27],[57.27,57.41],[57.41,57.78],[57.78,57.93],[57.93,58.52],[58.52,58.66],[58.66,58.88],[58.88,59.18],[59.18,59.62]]},{"el":"s0","text":"El boicot duró 381 días, sostenido por un sistema de viajes compartidos que movía a miles de personas al día.","start":60.37,"end":68.81,"words":[[60.39,60.53],[60.53,60.95],[60.95,61.23],[61.23,62.84],[62.84,63.26],[63.5,64.13],[64.13,64.34],[64.34,64.48],[64.48,64.97],[64.97,65.11],[65.11,65.53],[65.53,66.3],[66.3,66.44],[66.44,66.86],[66.86,66.93],[66.93,67.28],[67.28,67.42],[67.42,67.98],[67.98,68.11],[68.11,68.46]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Lo que finalmente puso fin a la segregación en los autobuses fue una demanda, Browder v. Gayle, que la Corte Suprema confirmó en noviembre de 1956.","start":69.16,"end":80.46,"words":[[69.19,69.33],[69.33,69.47],[69.47,70.16],[70.16,70.43],[70.43,70.64],[70.64,70.71],[70.71,70.85],[70.85,71.61],[71.61,71.74],[71.74,71.95],[71.95,72.57],[72.57,72.78],[72.78,72.98],[72.98,73.53],[73.78,74.26],[74.26,74.47],[74.81,75.22],[75.46,75.6],[75.6,75.74],[75.74,76.08],[76.08,76.57],[76.57,77.12],[77.12,77.26],[77.26,77.88],[77.88,78.01],[78.01,80.01]]},{"el":"s0","text":"El boicot mantuvo la presión y a la comunidad unida mientras el caso avanzaba en los tribunales.","start":80.81,"end":87.51,"words":[[80.83,80.99],[80.99,81.45],[81.45,82.0],[82.0,82.15],[82.15,82.7],[82.7,82.78],[82.78,82.86],[82.86,83.01],[83.01,83.71],[83.71,84.1],[84.1,84.73],[84.73,84.88],[84.88,85.19],[85.19,85.82],[85.82,85.97],[85.97,86.21],[86.21,87.06]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Brown v. Board: una estrategia legal de 20 años","start":88.41,"end":92.1,"words":[[88.44,88.77],[88.77,88.97],[89.3,89.7],[89.93,90.13],[90.13,90.79],[90.79,91.12],[91.12,91.26],[91.26,91.66],[91.66,91.92]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los abogados de la NAACP no empezaron por las escuelas primarias.","start":92.8,"end":96.82,"words":[[92.8,93.0],[93.0,93.54],[93.54,93.67],[93.67,93.8],[93.8,94.14],[94.14,94.27],[94.27,94.87],[94.87,95.07],[95.07,95.27],[95.27,95.81],[95.81,96.48]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Charles Hamilton Houston y su alumno Thurgood Marshall atacaron primero las escuelas de posgrado y de derecho segregadas, donde la desigualdad era más fácil de probar: Murray v. Pearson (1936), Gaines (1938), Sweatt v. Painter (1950).","start":97.17,"end":115.6,"words":[[97.19,97.64],[97.64,98.1],[98.1,98.49],[98.49,98.56],[98.56,98.69],[98.69,99.08],[99.08,99.54],[99.54,99.93],[99.93,100.45],[100.45,100.91],[100.91,101.11],[101.11,101.63],[101.63,101.76],[101.76,102.28],[102.28,102.35],[102.35,102.48],[102.48,102.94],[102.94,103.65],[103.88,104.21],[104.21,104.34],[104.34,105.06],[105.06,105.25],[105.25,105.45],[105.45,105.78],[105.78,105.91],[105.91,106.36],[106.59,106.92],[106.92,107.12],[107.44,107.9],[107.9,109.66],[109.89,110.28],[110.28,112.11],[112.34,112.73],[112.73,112.93],[113.25,113.71],[113.71,115.28]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Cada victoria sentó un precedente hasta que, en 1954, Brown v. Board of Education anuló el principio de “separados pero iguales”.","start":115.95,"end":125.92,"words":[[115.98,116.25],[116.25,116.78],[116.78,117.11],[117.11,117.24],[117.24,117.9],[117.9,118.17],[118.17,118.37],[118.6,118.73],[118.73,120.79],[121.02,121.35],[121.35,121.55],[121.88,122.21],[122.21,122.34],[122.34,122.94],[122.94,123.27],[123.27,123.4],[123.4,124.0],[124.0,124.13],[124.13,124.73],[124.73,124.99],[124.99,125.52]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Las sentadas: entrenamiento y disciplina","start":126.82,"end":130.43,"words":[[126.85,127.12],[127.12,127.95],[128.27,129.46],[129.46,129.55],[129.55,130.38]]},{"el":"s2","text":"El 1 de febrero de 1960, cuatro estudiantes de North Carolina A&T se sentaron en la barra de un Woolworth's de Greensboro reservada para blancos.","start":131.13,"end":141.11,"words":[[131.15,131.28],[131.28,131.49],[131.49,131.62],[131.62,132.1],[132.1,132.24],[132.24,133.74],[133.98,134.38],[134.38,135.13],[135.13,135.27],[135.27,135.54],[135.54,136.09],[136.09,136.36],[136.36,136.5],[136.5,137.04],[137.04,137.18],[137.18,137.31],[137.31,137.59],[137.59,137.72],[137.72,137.86],[137.86,138.47],[138.47,138.61],[138.61,139.29],[139.29,139.91],[139.91,140.18],[140.18,140.72]]},{"el":"s2","text":"En pocas semanas, las sentadas se extendieron a decenas de ciudades.","start":141.46,"end":146.56,"words":[[141.47,141.62],[141.62,141.98],[141.98,142.56],[142.82,143.04],[143.04,143.62],[143.62,143.77],[143.77,144.64],[144.64,144.71],[144.71,145.22],[145.22,145.37],[145.37,146.03]]},{"el":"s2","text":"En Nashville, los estudiantes se entrenaron durante meses en los talleres de no violencia de James Lawson, ensayando cómo aguantar insultos y golpes sin devolverlos.","start":146.91,"end":158.0,"words":[[146.94,147.08],[147.08,147.72],[147.98,148.19],[148.19,148.98],[148.98,149.12],[149.12,149.84],[149.84,150.34],[150.34,150.69],[150.69,150.84],[150.84,151.05],[151.05,151.62],[151.62,151.77],[151.77,151.91],[151.91,152.55],[152.55,152.7],[152.7,153.06],[153.06,153.56],[153.81,154.45],[154.45,154.74],[154.74,155.31],[155.31,155.88],[155.88,155.95],[155.95,156.38],[156.38,156.6],[156.6,157.46]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Junto con un boicot al centro de la ciudad, lograron que las barras se desegregaran en mayo.","start":158.35,"end":164.35,"words":[[158.39,158.74],[158.74,158.96],[158.96,159.1],[159.1,159.52],[159.52,159.67],[159.67,160.09],[160.09,160.24],[160.24,160.38],[160.38,160.88],[161.13,161.7],[161.7,161.84],[161.84,162.05],[162.05,162.41],[162.41,162.55],[162.55,163.41],[163.41,163.55],[163.55,163.91]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Ese abril, Ella Baker ayudó a los estudiantes a fundar el Comité Coordinador Estudiantil No Violento (SNCC).","start":164.7,"end":172.56,"words":[[164.75,164.97],[164.97,165.42],[165.68,165.98],[165.98,166.35],[166.35,166.72],[166.72,166.8],[166.8,167.02],[167.02,167.84],[167.84,167.91],[167.91,168.36],[168.36,168.51],[168.51,168.96],[168.96,169.77],[169.77,170.59],[170.59,170.74],[170.74,171.34],[171.34,172.16]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Su principio: “La gente fuerte no necesita líderes fuertes”.","start":172.91,"end":177.1,"words":[[172.94,173.08],[173.08,173.78],[174.02,174.16],[174.16,174.51],[174.51,174.93],[174.93,175.07],[175.07,175.63],[175.63,176.12],[176.12,176.68]]},{"el":"h3","text":"De Birmingham a la Ley de Derechos Civiles: crisis, coalición, cabildeo","start":178.0,"end":183.73,"words":[[178.02,178.18],[178.18,178.91],[178.91,178.99],[178.99,179.15],[179.15,179.39],[179.39,179.56],[179.56,180.2],[180.2,180.85],[181.14,181.7],[181.99,182.79],[183.08,183.73]]},{"el":"s3","text":"En la primavera de 1963, los organizadores de Birmingham combinaron marchas, un boicot a las tiendas del centro y la Cruzada de los Niños.","start":184.43,"end":195.19,"words":[[184.45,184.6],[184.6,184.74],[184.74,185.39],[185.39,185.54],[185.54,187.48],[187.74,187.95],[187.95,188.89],[188.89,189.03],[189.03,189.68],[189.68,190.41],[190.41,190.98],[191.23,191.38],[191.38,191.81],[191.81,191.88],[191.88,192.1],[192.1,192.61],[192.61,192.82],[192.82,193.25],[193.25,193.33],[193.33,193.47],[193.47,193.98],[193.98,194.12],[194.12,194.34],[194.34,194.77]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Las imágenes televisadas de perros policías y mangueras de bomberos contra niños obligaron al país a enfrentar la realidad.","start":195.54,"end":203.7,"words":[[195.55,195.77],[195.77,196.36],[196.36,197.17],[197.17,197.31],[197.31,197.68],[197.68,198.34],[198.34,198.41],[198.41,199.0],[199.0,199.15],[199.15,199.73],[199.73,200.17],[200.17,200.54],[200.54,201.2],[201.2,201.35],[201.35,201.64],[201.64,201.71],[201.71,202.37],[202.37,202.52],[202.52,203.18]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El 11 de junio, el presidente Kennedy propuso una ley de derechos civiles.","start":204.05,"end":209.12,"words":[[204.06,204.19],[204.19,204.46],[204.46,204.6],[204.6,205.01],[205.24,205.38],[205.38,206.06],[206.06,206.53],[206.53,207.01],[207.01,207.21],[207.21,207.42],[207.42,207.55],[207.55,208.09],[208.09,208.64]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La Marcha sobre Washington de ese agosto reunió a unas 250,000 personas.","start":209.47,"end":216.08,"words":[[209.52,209.66],[209.66,210.07],[210.07,210.42],[210.42,211.04],[211.04,211.18],[211.18,211.39],[211.39,211.8],[211.8,212.22],[212.22,212.29],[212.29,212.56],[212.56,214.99],[214.99,215.61]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La ley todavía tenía que pasar por el Congreso.","start":216.43,"end":219.96,"words":[[216.46,216.61],[216.61,216.84],[216.84,217.45],[217.45,217.9],[217.9,218.05],[218.05,218.43],[218.43,218.66],[218.66,218.81],[218.81,219.5]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La Leadership Conference on Civil Rights coordinó a iglesias, sindicatos y grupos cívicos para presionar a cada senador, y el cabildero de la NAACP Clarence Mitchell estaba tan presente que lo llamaban “el senador 101”.","start":220.31,"end":234.3,"words":[[220.31,220.45],[220.45,221.09],[221.09,221.81],[221.81,221.95],[221.95,222.31],[222.31,222.66],[222.66,223.23],[223.23,223.31],[223.31,223.95],[224.2,224.91],[224.91,224.98],[224.98,225.41],[225.41,225.91],[225.91,226.2],[226.2,226.84],[226.84,226.91],[226.91,227.2],[227.2,227.77],[228.02,228.09],[228.09,228.23],[228.23,228.88],[228.88,229.02],[229.02,229.16],[229.16,229.52],[229.52,230.09],[230.09,230.59],[230.59,231.02],[231.02,231.23],[231.23,231.8],[231.8,231.95],[231.95,232.09],[232.09,232.59],[232.59,232.73],[232.73,233.23],[233.23,233.95]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El Senado rompió un obstruccionismo (filibuster) el 10 de junio de 1964, y el presidente Johnson firmó la Ley de Derechos Civiles el 2 de julio.","start":234.65,"end":246.51,"words":[[234.67,234.82],[234.82,235.27],[235.27,235.72],[235.72,235.87],[235.87,237.0],[237.0,237.75],[238.01,238.16],[238.16,238.46],[238.46,238.61],[238.61,238.99],[238.99,239.14],[239.14,241.32],[241.58,241.65],[241.65,241.81],[241.81,242.56],[242.56,243.01],[243.01,243.38],[243.38,243.53],[243.53,243.76],[243.76,243.91],[243.91,244.51],[244.51,245.04],[245.04,245.19],[245.19,245.41],[245.41,245.56],[245.56,246.01]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Selma: primero, años de organización local","start":247.41,"end":250.27,"words":[[247.44,247.82],[248.05,248.56],[248.78,249.03],[249.03,249.16],[249.16,249.93],[249.93,250.24]]},{"el":"s4","text":"El Domingo Sangriento de 1965 pareció repentino.","start":250.97,"end":255.56,"words":[[250.99,251.12],[251.12,251.57],[251.57,252.28],[252.28,252.41],[252.41,254.15],[254.15,254.6],[254.6,255.24]]},{"el":"s4","text":"No lo fue.","start":255.91,"end":257.01,"words":[[255.93,256.07],[256.07,256.21],[256.21,256.48]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Los organizadores del SNCC trabajaban en Selma desde 1963, con campañas de registro de votantes y ganándose la confianza familia por familia.","start":257.36,"end":269.01,"words":[[257.38,257.6],[257.6,258.56],[258.56,258.78],[258.78,259.52],[259.52,260.26],[260.26,260.41],[260.41,260.78],[260.78,261.14],[261.14,263.14],[263.4,263.62],[263.62,264.21],[264.21,264.36],[264.36,264.95],[264.95,265.1],[265.1,265.69],[265.69,265.76],[265.76,266.43],[266.43,266.58],[266.58,267.24],[267.24,267.76],[267.76,267.98],[267.98,268.57]]},{"el":"s4","text":"El Verano de la Libertad de 1964 llevó a Misisipi a unos 1,000 voluntarios, la mayoría estudiantes universitarios blancos, y el Partido Demócrata por la Libertad de Misisipi de Fannie Lou Hamer desafió a la delegación totalmente blanca en la convención demócrata de 1964 ante la televisión nacional.","start":269.36,"end":293.59,"words":[[269.37,269.52],[269.52,269.97],[269.97,270.12],[270.12,270.26],[270.26,270.86],[270.86,271.01],[271.01,273.09],[273.09,273.38],[273.38,273.46],[273.46,274.05],[274.05,274.13],[274.13,274.42],[274.42,275.84],[275.84,276.73],[276.99,277.14],[277.14,277.73],[277.73,278.55],[278.55,279.59],[279.59,280.18],[280.44,280.52],[280.52,280.67],[280.67,281.19],[281.19,281.85],[281.85,282.08],[282.08,282.23],[282.23,282.82],[282.82,282.97],[282.97,283.56],[283.56,283.71],[283.71,284.16],[284.16,284.38],[284.38,284.68],[284.68,285.2],[285.2,285.27],[285.27,285.42],[285.42,286.16],[286.16,286.91],[286.91,287.35],[287.35,287.5],[287.5,287.65],[287.65,288.39],[288.39,289.06],[289.06,289.21],[289.21,291.29],[291.29,291.59],[291.59,291.73],[291.73,292.48],[292.48,293.15]]},{"el":"s4","text":"(Ver el módulo sobre el voto.)","start":293.94,"end":296.46,"words":[[293.97,294.22],[294.22,294.38],[294.38,294.87],[294.87,295.27],[295.27,295.44],[295.44,295.84]]},{"el":"h5","text":"¿La disrupción ayuda o perjudica?","start":297.36,"end":299.83,"words":[[297.39,297.53],[297.53,298.23],[298.23,298.57],[298.57,298.64],[298.64,299.34]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Historiadores y politólogos todavía discuten qué tácticas cambiaron la opinión pública.","start":300.53,"end":306.08,"words":[[300.55,301.38],[301.38,301.44],[301.44,302.2],[302.2,302.74],[302.74,303.29],[303.29,303.43],[303.43,303.97],[303.97,304.59],[304.59,304.73],[304.73,305.2],[305.2,305.75]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Un estudio de 2020 de Omar Wasow encontró que las protestas no violentas de los años 60 aumentaron el apoyo a los derechos civiles, mientras que las que se volvieron violentas empujaron a algunos votantes blancos hacia candidatos de “ley y orden” en 1968.","start":306.43,"end":325.49,"words":[[306.46,306.62],[306.62,307.15],[307.15,307.3],[307.3,308.21],[308.21,308.36],[308.36,308.66],[308.66,309.04],[309.04,309.65],[309.65,309.8],[309.8,310.03],[310.03,310.71],[310.71,310.87],[310.87,311.55],[311.55,311.7],[311.7,311.93],[311.93,312.23],[312.23,312.76],[312.76,313.52],[313.52,313.67],[313.67,314.05],[314.05,314.13],[314.13,314.36],[314.36,314.96],[314.96,315.57],[315.84,316.44],[316.44,316.59],[316.59,316.82],[316.82,316.97],[316.97,317.12],[317.12,317.81],[317.81,318.49],[318.49,319.17],[319.17,319.25],[319.25,319.78],[319.78,320.39],[320.39,320.92],[320.92,321.22],[321.22,321.98],[321.98,322.13],[322.13,322.36],[322.36,322.44],[322.44,322.82],[322.82,322.97],[322.97,325.09]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Otros sostienen que la amenaza de grupos más militantes y de la autodefensa armada (como los Deacons for Defense) hizo que las autoridades estuvieran más dispuestas a negociar con los líderes no violentos.","start":325.84,"end":338.94,"words":[[325.87,326.24],[326.24,326.9],[326.9,327.05],[327.05,327.2],[327.2,327.71],[327.71,327.86],[327.86,328.3],[328.3,328.52],[328.52,329.26],[329.26,329.34],[329.34,329.48],[329.48,329.63],[329.63,330.44],[330.44,330.89],[330.89,331.18],[331.18,331.4],[331.4,331.92],[331.92,332.14],[332.14,332.66],[332.92,333.14],[333.14,333.29],[333.29,333.51],[333.51,334.32],[334.32,335.06],[335.06,335.28],[335.28,336.02],[336.02,336.09],[336.09,336.68],[336.68,336.9],[336.9,337.13],[337.13,337.64],[337.64,337.79],[337.79,338.53]]},{"el":"s5","text":"La mayoría coincide en que la disciplina, las demandas claras y una amplia simpatía pública fueron esenciales.","start":339.29,"end":347.03,"words":[[339.29,339.44],[339.44,340.04],[340.04,340.64],[340.64,340.79],[340.79,340.94],[340.94,341.09],[341.09,341.83],[342.1,342.32],[342.32,342.92],[342.92,343.37],[343.37,343.44],[343.44,343.66],[343.66,344.19],[344.19,344.86],[344.86,345.38],[345.38,345.83],[345.83,346.65]]},{"el":"h6","text":"Victorias recientes que esta campaña puede copiar","start":347.93,"end":351.13,"words":[[347.97,348.63],[348.63,349.29],[349.29,349.43],[349.43,349.73],[349.73,350.24],[350.24,350.61],[350.61,351.05]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La Ley CAREN de San Francisco pasó de su presentación a un voto unánime en unos tres meses en 2020.","start":351.83,"end":358.56,"words":[[351.84,351.98],[351.98,352.2],[352.2,352.55],[352.55,352.69],[352.69,352.91],[352.91,353.55],[353.55,353.83],[353.83,353.97],[353.97,354.11],[354.11,354.97],[354.97,355.04],[355.04,355.18],[355.18,355.46],[355.46,355.96],[355.96,356.1],[356.1,356.39],[356.39,356.67],[356.67,357.03],[357.03,357.17],[357.17,358.09]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La ley de Oregón se aprobó en 2019 porque una legisladora estatal, Janelle Bynum, sufrió una llamada a la policía mientras hacía campaña puerta a puerta y contó su historia.","start":358.91,"end":371.04,"words":[[358.93,359.08],[359.08,359.29],[359.29,359.44],[359.44,359.87],[359.87,360.02],[360.02,360.45],[360.45,360.59],[360.59,361.74],[361.74,362.1],[362.1,362.32],[362.32,363.11],[363.11,363.69],[363.94,364.45],[364.45,364.88],[365.13,365.64],[365.64,365.85],[365.85,366.28],[366.28,366.36],[366.36,366.5],[366.5,367.08],[367.08,367.65],[367.65,368.01],[368.01,368.52],[368.52,368.95],[368.95,369.02],[369.02,369.45],[369.45,369.53],[369.53,369.89],[369.89,370.03],[370.03,370.61]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La campaña “Ban the box” se extendió ciudad por ciudad antes de que los estados la adoptaran.","start":371.39,"end":377.21,"words":[[371.39,371.53],[371.53,372.04],[372.04,372.25],[372.25,372.4],[372.4,372.69],[372.69,372.83],[372.83,373.49],[373.49,373.92],[373.92,374.14],[374.14,374.57],[374.57,374.94],[374.94,375.08],[375.08,375.23],[375.23,375.44],[375.44,375.95],[375.95,376.1],[376.1,376.82]]},{"el":"s6","text":"En 2018, los votantes de Florida devolvieron el derecho al voto a más de un millón de personas mediante una iniciativa ciudadana que obtuvo el 64.6% de los votos.","start":377.56,"end":390.32,"words":[[377.58,377.72],[377.72,378.92],[379.16,379.37],[379.37,379.93],[379.93,380.07],[380.07,380.56],[380.56,381.33],[381.33,381.47],[381.47,381.96],[381.96,382.1],[382.1,382.38],[382.38,382.45],[382.45,382.67],[382.67,382.81],[382.81,382.95],[382.95,383.37],[383.37,383.51],[383.51,384.07],[384.07,384.63],[384.63,384.84],[384.84,385.54],[385.54,386.17],[386.17,386.31],[386.31,386.73],[386.73,386.87],[386.87,389.11],[389.11,389.25],[389.25,389.46],[389.46,389.88]]},{"el":"s6","text":"El patrón: empezar en lo local, contar historias reales y luego llevarlo al estado y al país.","start":390.67,"end":396.9,"words":[[390.69,390.83],[390.83,391.32],[391.56,392.05],[392.05,392.19],[392.19,392.33],[392.33,392.75],[392.99,393.41],[393.41,393.96],[393.96,394.38],[394.38,394.45],[394.45,394.8],[394.8,395.29],[395.29,395.43],[395.43,395.84],[395.84,395.91],[395.91,396.05],[396.05,396.4]]},{"el":"h7","text":"La estrategia para una Ley CAREN federal","start":397.8,"end":400.27,"words":[[397.83,397.97],[397.97,398.69],[398.69,398.98],[398.98,399.19],[399.19,399.41],[399.41,399.77],[399.77,400.27]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Mapea el poder.","start":400.97,"end":402.25,"words":[[400.98,401.3],[401.3,401.43],[401.43,401.81]]},{"el":"s7","text":"¿Quién decide?","start":402.6,"end":403.56,"words":[[402.62,402.79],[402.79,403.09]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Los Comités Judiciales de la Cámara y el Senado estudian el proyecto; tus propios miembros lo votan.","start":403.91,"end":410.39,"words":[[403.91,404.12],[404.12,404.6],[404.6,405.29],[405.29,405.43],[405.43,405.57],[405.57,405.98],[405.98,406.05],[406.05,406.19],[406.19,406.61],[406.61,407.16],[407.16,407.3],[407.3,407.92],[408.16,408.37],[408.37,408.85],[408.85,409.41],[409.41,409.54],[409.54,409.96]]},{"el":"s7","text":"La capa de aliados del mapa los muestra.","start":410.74,"end":413.88,"words":[[410.77,410.92],[410.92,411.23],[411.23,411.39],[411.39,411.93],[411.93,412.16],[412.16,412.47],[412.47,412.7],[412.7,413.32]]},{"el":"s7","text":"(Misión: Mapea quién decide.)","start":414.23,"end":416.65,"words":[[414.25,414.76],[415.02,415.38],[415.38,415.67],[415.67,416.18]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Gana primero en lo local.","start":417.0,"end":418.69,"words":[[417.03,417.26],[417.26,417.66],[417.66,417.78],[417.78,417.89],[417.89,418.24]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Las resoluciones de concejos municipales y las leyes estatales sientan precedentes y le muestran al Congreso una ola.","start":419.04,"end":426.75,"words":[[419.06,419.28],[419.28,420.16],[420.16,420.31],[420.31,420.9],[420.9,421.7],[421.7,421.77],[421.77,421.99],[421.99,422.36],[422.36,423.02],[423.02,423.53],[423.53,424.34],[424.34,424.41],[424.41,424.56],[424.56,425.14],[425.14,425.29],[425.29,425.88],[425.88,426.1],[426.1,426.39]]},{"el":"s7","text":"(Misión: Gana una resolución local.)","start":427.1,"end":429.59,"words":[[427.13,427.57],[427.8,428.05],[428.05,428.24],[428.24,428.87],[428.87,429.25]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Construye una coalición inesperada.","start":429.94,"end":432.81,"words":[[429.95,430.57],[430.57,430.77],[430.77,431.39],[431.39,432.15]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Iglesias, sindicatos, grupos de derechos civiles, grupos asiático-americanos, latinos e indígenas, y negocios que no quieren que acosen a sus clientes.","start":433.16,"end":443.56,"words":[[433.21,433.82],[434.06,434.8],[435.04,435.45],[435.45,435.59],[435.59,436.13],[436.13,436.67],[436.91,437.32],[437.32,438.61],[438.85,439.33],[439.33,439.39],[439.39,440.08],[440.31,440.38],[440.38,440.93],[440.93,441.06],[441.06,441.2],[441.2,441.61],[441.61,441.74],[441.74,442.15],[442.15,442.22],[442.22,442.42],[442.42,443.1]]},{"el":"s7","text":"(Misión: Construye una coalición.)","start":443.91,"end":446.86,"words":[[443.94,444.49],[444.77,445.48],[445.48,445.72],[445.72,446.5]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Cuenta historias respaldadas por datos.","start":447.21,"end":449.83,"words":[[447.23,447.62],[447.62,448.15],[448.15,448.88],[448.88,449.07],[449.07,449.47]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Las historias personales mueven a los legisladores; los datos de resultados del 911 y de la BJS protegen esas historias para que no las descarten.","start":450.18,"end":461.01,"words":[[450.2,450.42],[450.42,451.02],[451.02,451.76],[451.76,452.2],[452.2,452.28],[452.28,452.5],[452.5,453.47],[453.72,453.95],[453.95,454.32],[454.32,454.47],[454.47,455.21],[455.21,455.43],[455.43,456.54],[456.54,456.62],[456.62,456.77],[456.77,456.92],[456.92,457.58],[457.58,458.18],[458.18,458.47],[458.47,459.07],[459.07,459.36],[459.36,459.51],[459.51,459.66],[459.66,459.88],[459.88,460.63]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Trabaja adentro y afuera a la vez.","start":461.36,"end":463.75,"words":[[461.36,461.85],[461.85,462.34],[462.34,462.41],[462.41,462.83],[462.83,462.9],[462.9,463.04],[463.04,463.32]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Reuniones con el personal y testimonios en audiencias, más presión pública: llamadas, columnas de opinión, eventos.","start":464.1,"end":471.02,"words":[[464.1,464.63],[464.63,464.81],[464.81,464.92],[464.92,465.39],[465.39,465.45],[465.45,466.09],[466.09,466.21],[466.21,466.85],[467.06,467.23],[467.23,467.64],[467.64,468.11],[468.32,468.79],[468.99,469.46],[469.46,469.58],[469.58,470.04],[470.25,470.72]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Capacita a la gente y sigue adelante.","start":471.37,"end":474.6,"words":[[471.39,472.05],[472.05,472.13],[472.13,472.29],[472.29,472.7],[472.7,472.78],[472.78,473.11],[473.11,473.84]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Los talleres convierten a quienes aprenden en organizadores.","start":474.95,"end":478.86,"words":[[474.97,475.17],[475.17,475.71],[475.71,476.39],[476.39,476.46],[476.46,476.86],[476.86,477.4],[477.4,477.54],[477.54,478.48]]},{"el":"s7","text":"La mayoría de las victorias tardan años, no semanas.","start":479.21,"end":482.79,"words":[[479.21,479.34],[479.34,479.86],[479.86,479.98],[479.98,480.18],[480.18,480.75],[480.75,481.14],[481.14,481.46],[481.68,481.81],[481.81,482.33]]}],"audio":"https://carenactmedia.blob.core.windows.net/audio/es/movements.male.a3fda21df7.mp3","bytes":1935047,"sha256":"a3fda21df75b5fc5bc2557ed54258a2c0fd314b717c69edd9cfeb474007bdf5f"}